  "note": "Election of the whole council (12 seats at large) on 18 September 1946; 18 candidates stood and 12 were returned (Belfast News-Letter, 19 September 1946, p. 5). There were 18 candidates. The nominations (Belfast News-Letter, 6 September 1946, p. 5) name A. G. Algeo, M. Cunningham, W. M'Kee Dunlop, R. Macafee, R. M'Ilroy, D. M'Kenna, J. P. Owens, J. M. Reith, G. C. Ashe, W. Baird, H. G. Campbell, J. Donaghy, J. Fullerton, A. Getty, T. W. M'Coubrey, J. M'Cracken, T. L. M'Elderry and J. M'Naul. Citation unconfirmed: the names were not all found on the cited page (verification 5 Nov 2026)."
